# The boundary of `child_usage`, as this crate ships it to a Nikaia program
# ([ADR-290](../../../docs/specification/adr/adr-290.md) D22, Part III 15.2).
#
# Drafted by `nikaia describe child_usage` and reviewed against `src/lib.rs`.
# The scope is #788's: the safe free functions that take no type parameter.
# An `unsafe fn` is left out, so a call to one stays NK1171. Methods and
# generic results are left out until #789. `nikaia.derived` beside this
# file records the sources it was reviewed against: a change to them
# makes `nikaia describe` refuse this file until it is reviewed again.
#
# crate: child_usage 0.1.0
version = 4

# A `std::process::Child` in, an `io::Result<Waited>` out: neither has a
# Nikaia type, so the signature claims nothing about them. The child is
# taken by value (`keeps`). The wait blocks the thread until the child
# ends (`wait4` on Unix), so it is not `sync`; it fails with an `io::Error`;
# what it touches and whether it locks are left fail-closed.
[fn."child_usage::wait"]
pub = true
keeps = ["child"]
throws = ["?"]
signature = "(child: ?) -> ?"
